    "c4": {
      "anchor": "p-the-editor-on-the-cloud",
      "kind": "phase",
      "label": "The Editor On The Cloud",
      "excerpt": "The Editor On The Cloud",
      "text": "2. fine if this is from the dev server for now if that makes things easier.  At some point very soon, I'm going to want to start editing with the editor -- so e.g. live reload may be helpful\n3. Don't worry about signin for now",
      "by": "owenoak",
      "at": "2026-11-09T04:15:42.411Z",
      "status": "answered",
      "replies": [
        {
          "by": "owenoak",
          "agent": "claude",
          "at": "2026-11-09T04:17:25.174Z",
          "html": "<p>Both folded into the plan above, which waits for your Accept.</p>\n<ul>\n  <li>The editor comes from the development server, with live reload, and test.spell.app becomes the editor outright.</li>\n  <li>No sign-in for now, which makes this much smaller:  Caddy picks by address, and the cloud doesn't change.</li>\n  <li><strong>Anyone on the house network who reaches test.spell.app edits as you.</strong>  The requests inbox for Claude sessions stays refused, so nobody can write to a session.</li>\n  <li>The production build and sign-in are a todo for before any public address.</li>\n</ul>"
        }
      ],
      "claim": {
